Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790611199999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": false, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790553599999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["Two long-duration two-sided ranges (bars 8-32 and 84-107) dominate much of the window, with heavy overlap.", "The immediate six bars (115-120) are a tight sideways group with upper wicks (bar 116 high 2786.81), a stall rather than fresh breakout.", "The window opens with a bear spike, so the 120-bar span is not uniformly bullish.", "Number of overlapping and doji-like bars in the middle reflects two-sided trade rather than a clean one-way trend throughout."], "evidence_for": ["Sequence of higher swing highs and higher lows from the 1368.42 low (bar 7) through the 2850 high (bar 114).", "The recent 2850 high exceeds the 2680 spike and the 2357-2557 range top, showing acceptance above prior consolidation.", "Several strong bull trend bars with wide range and close near high (bars 81, 82, 83, 104, 111, 114).", "Price holds well above the 1821-1974 range that contained bars 54-80, and the last consolidation sits high in the window."], "missing_information": ["No pre-window bars, so whether 1368.42 or 2850 marks a major higher-timeframe swing level is unknown.", "No volume profile or order-flow context; only closed OHLC bars are available.", "No declared reference levels from outside the supplied 120-bar window."], "observations": ["120-bar D1 window opens near 2006 and sells off in seven consecutive lower bars to a 1368.42 low, a climax bear spike of roughly one-third.", "Bars 8-32 form a two-sided base between 1512.91 and 1845.09 with heavy overlap, doji-like bars, and no sustained directional follow-through.", "Bars 33-53 lift with higher swing highs and higher lows from 1597.72 to 1954.36, a bull leg punctuated by short two- to four-bar pullbacks.", "Bars 54-80 return to a broad two-sided range roughly 1821.49-1974.46, so much of the middle of the window is range rather than one-way trend.", "Bar 81 is an explosive bull trend bar (open 1916.51, close 2252.16) that begins an approximately three-bar bull spike to a 2771 high.", "Bars 84-107 consolidate in a broad range around 2357.18-2557.46, including a single spike high of 2680 at bar 104 that is not held.", "Bars 108-114 break above that range to a new window high of 2850, with large bull bars at bars 111 and 114.", "Bars 115-120 form a tight consolidation between 2633.31 and 2786.81 with clustered closes near 2685-2695, a pause just below the 2850 high.", "Final-third closes sit in the upper portion of the window's overall range, consistent with higher lows and higher highs since the bar-7 low."], "phase": "channel", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Opening bear spike: seven consecutive lower bars from a 2035.94 high to a 1368.42 low with large bear ranges and closes near the low.", "end_time_ms": 1780703999999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780185600000, "upper_boundary": "2035.94"}, {"description": "Two-sided base after the sell-off; overlapping bars and repeated tests between the 1512.91 low and the 1845.09 spike high of bar 16.", "end_time_ms": 1782950399999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1512.91", "start_time_ms": 1780704000000, "upper_boundary": "1845.09"}, {"description": "Bull leg with higher highs and higher lows from 1597.72 to 1954.36, interrupted by tight pullbacks.", "end_time_ms": 1784851199999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "1597.72", "start_time_ms": 1782950400000, "upper_boundary": "1954.36"}, {"description": "Broad two-sided range roughly 1821.49-1974.46 that overlaps the prior bull leg, containing many doji and overlapping bars.", "end_time_ms": 1787183999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1821.49", "start_time_ms": 1784851200000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Explosive three-bar bull spike out of the prior range, led by the very large bar 81; high reaches 2771.", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Broad consolidation around 2357.18-2557.46 after the spike; a lone spike high of 2680 at bar 104 is rejected and price falls back inside.", "end_time_ms": 1789343999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2557.46"}, {"description": "Bull leg breaking above the prior range to a new window high of 2850, with large bull bars at bars 111 and 114.", "end_time_ms": 1790035199999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789430400000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Tight six-bar consolidation below the 2850 high between 2633.31 and 2786.81, with clustered closes and an upper-wick bar 116.", "end_time_ms": 1790553599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1790035200000, "upper_boundary": "2786.81"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Sustained closes back inside the 2357.18-2557.46 range would move the read back toward trading-range.", "A close below the 2633.31 consolidation low would deepen the pullback and weaken the channel reading.", "A decisive break and hold above 2850 with follow-through would reinforce the bull-trend and channel classification.", "A close below the 1905.63 spike low area would negate the bull breakout and shift toward transition-unclear."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "unclear", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": false, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790611199999, "directional_pressure": "balanced", "evidence_against": ["The larger context is a strong bull leg from 2358.62 to 2850, so the current overlap could be a bull flag rather than a mature range.", "The higher-low sequence since 2358.62 remains intact, with the 2633.31 low (bar 94) still far above the prior swing low.", "Bar 76 is an unusually strong bull spike, showing aggressive buying that could resume.", "The final two bars defended the range lows (2636.28/2637) and closed strong at 2677.55, showing demand at support rather than a broken range."], "evidence_for": ["About 43 bars of overlapping, two-sided trade since the 2850 high with no sustained break of either boundary.", "Descending highs (2804.59, 2786.81, 2740.42, 2717.27, 2697.02) against holding lows produce a contracting, balanced range profile.", "Repeated tests of the 2633-2668 support zone fail to follow through to the downside, and repeated forays toward 2740+ fail to follow through to the upside.", "Volume and bar range contract to fresh lows in the last ~20 bars, behavior typical of a range middle/late rather than an active trend.", "The 2850 high has not been exceeded since bar 76 despite roughly 43 subsequent bars."], "missing_information": ["No higher-timeframe (D1) or longer history is supplied; the broader trend beyond this 120-bar H4 window is unknown.", "Order-flow/positioning data beyond bar volume is unavailable, so the durability of the 2633-2668 support and 2740-2804 resistance cannot be confirmed.", "Whether the 2850 bar-76 high is a completed bull climax or an interim high cannot be determined without subsequent bars.", "No measured-move or prior-swing context outside the window is available to size the range."], "observations": ["120 closed H4 bars; window opens at 2497.6 and the final bar closes at 2677.55.", "Early window (bars 0-42) is choppy and two-sided: a single-bar spike to 2680 on bar 17 reversed, and price ultimately ground down to a window low of 2358.62 on bar 42.", "Mid-window holds a strong bull leg from the 2358.62 low to a 2850 window high on bar 76 (roughly +21%); bars 59, 60 and 76 are large-range bull bars.", "Bar 76 is an outsi