Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790625599999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": false, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790553599999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["Two long-duration two-sided ranges (bars 8-32 and 84-107) dominate much of the window, with heavy overlap.", "The immediate six bars (115-120) are a tight sideways group with upper wicks (bar 116 high 2786.81), a stall rather than fresh breakout.", "The window opens with a bear spike, so the 120-bar span is not uniformly bullish.", "Number of overlapping and doji-like bars in the middle reflects two-sided trade rather than a clean one-way trend throughout."], "evidence_for": ["Sequence of higher swing highs and higher lows from the 1368.42 low (bar 7) through the 2850 high (bar 114).", "The recent 2850 high exceeds the 2680 spike and the 2357-2557 range top, showing acceptance above prior consolidation.", "Several strong bull trend bars with wide range and close near high (bars 81, 82, 83, 104, 111, 114).", "Price holds well above the 1821-1974 range that contained bars 54-80, and the last consolidation sits high in the window."], "missing_information": ["No pre-window bars, so whether 1368.42 or 2850 marks a major higher-timeframe swing level is unknown.", "No volume profile or order-flow context; only closed OHLC bars are available.", "No declared reference levels from outside the supplied 120-bar window."], "observations": ["120-bar D1 window opens near 2006 and sells off in seven consecutive lower bars to a 1368.42 low, a climax bear spike of roughly one-third.", "Bars 8-32 form a two-sided base between 1512.91 and 1845.09 with heavy overlap, doji-like bars, and no sustained directional follow-through.", "Bars 33-53 lift with higher swing highs and higher lows from 1597.72 to 1954.36, a bull leg punctuated by short two- to four-bar pullbacks.", "Bars 54-80 return to a broad two-sided range roughly 1821.49-1974.46, so much of the middle of the window is range rather than one-way trend.", "Bar 81 is an explosive bull trend bar (open 1916.51, close 2252.16) that begins an approximately three-bar bull spike to a 2771 high.", "Bars 84-107 consolidate in a broad range around 2357.18-2557.46, including a single spike high of 2680 at bar 104 that is not held.", "Bars 108-114 break above that range to a new window high of 2850, with large bull bars at bars 111 and 114.", "Bars 115-120 form a tight consolidation between 2633.31 and 2786.81 with clustered closes near 2685-2695, a pause just below the 2850 high.", "Final-third closes sit in the upper portion of the window's overall range, consistent with higher lows and higher highs since the bar-7 low."], "phase": "channel", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Opening bear spike: seven consecutive lower bars from a 2035.94 high to a 1368.42 low with large bear ranges and closes near the low.", "end_time_ms": 1780703999999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780185600000, "upper_boundary": "2035.94"}, {"description": "Two-sided base after the sell-off; overlapping bars and repeated tests between the 1512.91 low and the 1845.09 spike high of bar 16.", "end_time_ms": 1782950399999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1512.91", "start_time_ms": 1780704000000, "upper_boundary": "1845.09"}, {"description": "Bull leg with higher highs and higher lows from 1597.72 to 1954.36, interrupted by tight pullbacks.", "end_time_ms": 1784851199999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "1597.72", "start_time_ms": 1782950400000, "upper_boundary": "1954.36"}, {"description": "Broad two-sided range roughly 1821.49-1974.46 that overlaps the prior bull leg, containing many doji and overlapping bars.", "end_time_ms": 1787183999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1821.49", "start_time_ms": 1784851200000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Explosive three-bar bull spike out of the prior range, led by the very large bar 81; high reaches 2771.", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Broad consolidation around 2357.18-2557.46 after the spike; a lone spike high of 2680 at bar 104 is rejected and price falls back inside.", "end_time_ms": 1789343999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2557.46"}, {"description": "Bull leg breaking above the prior range to a new window high of 2850, with large bull bars at bars 111 and 114.", "end_time_ms": 1790035199999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789430400000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Tight six-bar consolidation below the 2850 high between 2633.31 and 2786.81, with clustered closes and an upper-wick bar 116.", "end_time_ms": 1790553599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1790035200000, "upper_boundary": "2786.81"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Sustained closes back inside the 2357.18-2557.46 range would move the read back toward trading-range.", "A close below the 2633.31 consolidation low would deepen the pullback and weaken the channel reading.", "A decisive break and hold above 2850 with follow-through would reinforce the bull-trend and channel classification.", "A close below the 1905.63 spike low area would negate the bull breakout and shift toward transition-unclear."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "unclear", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": false, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790625599999, "directional_pressure": "balanced", "evidence_against": ["The window contains a strong, sustained bull leg from 2358.62 to 2850 (+~21%) with clear higher highs and higher lows, which could describe a bull trend rather than a range.", "The recent range holds above the ~2604 midpoint of that bull leg, a configuration often seen in a bull flag that resumes upward.", "Several large bull bars (bars 59, 60, 76, 100) show genuine buying pressure, not purely mechanical two-sided trade.", "The recent lower low (2633.31 vs 2648.49) is marginal, not a decisive breakdown, so the range boundary has not been clearly violated.", "A large part of the window is directional (bear leg then bull leg), so the sideways behavior may be a pause within a trend rather than the dominant regime."], "evidence_for": ["The most recent ~44 bars (bar 77 onward) are two-sided and overlapping, with repeated failed boundary tests on both sides rather than sustained trend closes.", "Recent highs descend (2850, 2804.59, 2740.42, 2717.27) while lows hold in a narrow 2633-2648 zone, a sideways rather than trending pattern.", "Multiple prior failed breakouts (bar 17 to 2680, bar 38 to 2609.02) show overhead supply and two-sided responsive behavior above the market.", "The last 20 bars round-tripped from ~2671 back to 2672.79, producing essentially no net directional progress.", "Bars in the recent range are small and heavily overlapping, typical of a trading range rather than a channel or spike."], "missing_information": ["No higher-timeframe (D1) structure supplied, so the position of this H4 range within a larger trend is inferred only from this window.", "Volume context is present as raw numbers only; no volume-profile or participation analysis is available to judge acceptance or rejection.", "Whether the 2850 spike (bar 76) marked an exhaustion climax cannot be confirmed without bars beyond the frozen window.", "No explicit measurement of prior swings outside the 120-bar window, so the range's relationship to older boundaries is unknown.", "The internal low at 2633.31 (bar 94) is a single-bar probe; whether it or 2636-2648 is the effective range floor is ambiguo